From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: tegra: skip unconfigured optional media sinks

The VI upstream graph parser accepts unconfigured optional GMSL inputs
after patch 0104, but media link construction still resolves every remote
endpoint before checking whether the local pad is a sink. The modular
transport overlay intentionally omits remote-endpoint on inputs without
a camera leaf. Parsing these placeholders fails, and an error from the
last endpoint can unregister an otherwise valid sparse capture channel.

For Maxim deserializers opting into compulab,allow-missing-links, classify
the local endpoint before remote resolution. Validate its port against
the actual media entity pad count, then skip only sink endpoints with no
remote-endpoint property. Configured inputs still require a resolvable
remote, including properties that are present but malformed or dangling.
Source/output endpoints retain their strict remote requirement.

Do not let a later endpoint overwrite a configured-link parsing failure
on an optional bridge. Return its error immediately and release the
iterator's endpoint reference on these new error exits. Ordinary graphs,
required Maxim graphs, serializer links and routing stay unchanged.

Prepared against NVIDIA Jetson Linux 39.2.1 after the ADI patches
0100 through 0104. No device-tree or sensor-mode changes are required.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CompuLab Tegra optional camera discovery]
Signed-off-by: Valentin Raevsky <valentin@compulab.co.il>
---
 drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 30 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/tegra/camera/vi/graph.c
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ static int tegra_vi_graph_build_one(struct tegra_channel *chan,
 	struct v4l2_fwnode_link link;
 	struct device_node *ep = NULL;
 	struct device_node *next;
+	bool optional_maxim;
 	int ret = 0;
 
 	if (!entity->subdev) {
@@ -70,6 +71,9 @@ static int tegra_vi_graph_build_one(struct tegra_channel *chan,
 	}
 
 	local = entity->entity;
+	optional_maxim = tegra_vi_graph_is_maxim_deserializer(entity->node) &&
+		of_property_read_bool(entity->node,
+				      "compulab,allow-missing-links");
 	dev_dbg(chan->vi->dev, "creating links for entity %s\n", local->name);
 
 	do {
@@ -82,6 +86,27 @@ static int tegra_vi_graph_build_one(struct tegra_channel *chan,
 
 		dev_dbg(chan->vi->dev, "processing endpoint %pOF\n",
 				ep);
+		if (optional_maxim) {
+			struct of_endpoint endpoint;
+
+			ret = of_graph_parse_endpoint(ep, &endpoint);
+			if (ret) {
+				of_node_put(ep);
+				return ret;
+			}
+			if (endpoint.port >= local->num_pads) {
+				dev_err(chan->vi->dev,
+					"invalid port number %u for %pOF\n",
+					endpoint.port, entity->node);
+				of_node_put(ep);
+				return -EINVAL;
+			}
+
+			/* A camera leaf configures only its optional input. */
+			if ((local->pads[endpoint.port].flags & MEDIA_PAD_FL_SINK) &&
+			    !of_find_property(ep, "remote-endpoint", NULL))
+				continue;
+		}
 #if defined(CONFIG_V4L2_FWNODE)
 		ret = v4l2_fwnode_parse_link(of_fwnode_handle(ep), &link);
 #else
@@ -91,6 +116,11 @@ static int tegra_vi_graph_build_one(struct tegra_channel *chan,
 		if (ret < 0) {
 			dev_err(chan->vi->dev,
 			"failed to parse link for %pOF\n", ep);
+			/* A configured optional input or any output stays strict. */
+			if (optional_maxim) {
+				of_node_put(ep);
+				return ret;
+			}
 			continue;
 		}
 
